WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.567 --> 00:00:04.934
-The president's lawyer went on
TV and basically admitted

00:00:04.934 --> 00:00:07.434
that his campaign might have
colluded with Russia.

00:00:07.434 --> 00:00:09.501
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:09.501 --> 00:00:10.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.934 --> 00:00:14.234
♪♪

00:00:14.234 --> 00:00:17.100
Every day, it gets harder to
defend Trump's actions

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.234
in the Russia investigation
which is why Trump

00:00:19.234 --> 00:00:23.133
cycles through more lawyers
than a "Law &amp; Order" marathon.

00:00:23.133 --> 00:00:25.901
"Oh, hey, that guy was a jogger
three episodes ago."

00:00:25.901 --> 00:00:27.300
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:29.400
In fact, this week, Trump's
nominee for Attorney General

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:31.534
William Barr was grilled
by Senators

00:00:31.534 --> 00:00:33.200
at his confirmation hearing
about the fact

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.367
that Trump
originally wanted Barr

00:00:35.367 --> 00:00:37.501
to be his private criminal
defense attorney,

00:00:37.501 --> 00:00:39.567
which would be an obvious
conflict of interest.

00:00:39.567 --> 00:00:41.701
But Barr said he met with Trump
once

00:00:41.701 --> 00:00:43.701
and then never heard back
from him.

00:00:43.701 --> 00:00:48.300
-It was a very brief meeting
where essentially the president

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:51.033
wanted to know -- he said,
"Oh, you know Bob Mueller.

00:00:51.033 --> 00:00:52.501
How well do you know Bob
Mueller?"

00:00:52.501 --> 00:00:54.567
I told him how well I knew Bob
Mueller,

00:00:54.567 --> 00:00:56.534
and he was interested in that,

00:00:56.534 --> 00:00:58.901
wanted to know, you know,
what I thought about

00:00:58.901 --> 00:01:01.267
Mueller's integrity and so forth
and so on.

00:01:01.267 --> 00:01:04.067
And I said,
"Bob is a straight shooter

00:01:04.067 --> 00:01:05.868
and should be dealt with
as such."

00:01:05.868 --> 00:01:07.601
So he asked me
for my phone number.

00:01:07.601 --> 00:01:10.667
I gave it to him, and I never
heard from him again.

00:01:10.667 --> 00:01:11.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.901 --> 00:01:14.300
-Well, it's obvious why.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:16.501
I mean, we've all seen
Trump's tweets.

00:01:16.501 --> 00:01:18.334
I mean...

00:01:18.334 --> 00:01:22.267
what are the odds he wrote down
a phone number correctly?

00:01:22.267 --> 00:01:28.033
[ As Trump ] Yeah, dial this --
213-55K-crying-emoji-8.

00:01:28.033 --> 00:01:29.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.167 --> 00:01:31.968
What do you mean
it's not ringing?

00:01:31.968 --> 00:01:33.534
[ Normal voice ] So Barr didn't
want to be Trump's lawyer.

00:01:33.534 --> 00:01:34.767
No respectable lawyer does.

00:01:34.767 --> 00:01:36.100
That's why Trump is stuck with

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:39.234
outer borough ambulance chasers
like Rudy Giuliani.

00:01:39.234 --> 00:01:43.067
Although Rudy doesn't really
look like he chases ambulances.

00:01:43.067 --> 00:01:45.767
They probably just follow him
when he goes out for a walk.

00:01:45.767 --> 00:01:47.567
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.567 --> 00:01:49.100
But apparently --

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:50.501
[ Applause ]

00:01:50.501 --> 00:01:54.634
But apparently, even Rudy is
having a hard time with the job,

00:01:54.634 --> 00:01:56.634
especially as
Special Counsel Robert Mueller

00:01:56.634 --> 00:01:58.167
prepares to issue
his final report.

00:01:58.167 --> 00:02:01.667
"Vanity Fair" reported yesterday
that Rudy fears that the report

00:02:01.667 --> 00:02:04.567
will be horrific for Trump
and that the mounting pressure

00:02:04.567 --> 00:02:07.467
has also strained Giuliani's
relationship with Trump.

00:02:07.467 --> 00:02:08.634
"Rudy hates the job.

00:02:08.634 --> 00:02:11.100
Trump is very hard
to deal with."

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:13.801
Oh, you're just
finding that out now?!

00:02:13.801 --> 00:02:14.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:16.934
Come on, Rudy,
you went into this job

00:02:16.934 --> 00:02:20.100
with your eyes wide open,
and I do mean wide open.

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:21.534
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.534 --> 00:02:24.834
You look like you just saw
a pretty lady in an old cartoon.

00:02:24.834 --> 00:02:26.667
[ Ah-oogah! ]

00:02:26.667 --> 00:02:29.200
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:34.667 --> 00:02:36.601
We spent a lot of time
on that today.

00:02:36.601 --> 00:02:38.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:40.267
And it really does seem like
the pressure of the job

00:02:40.267 --> 00:02:42.033
is getting to Rudy
because last night,

00:02:42.033 --> 00:02:43.501
he went on CNN and blurted out

00:02:43.501 --> 00:02:46.367
another one of his trademark
accidental confessions.

00:02:46.367 --> 00:02:48.968
Rudy was interviewed
by CNN's Chris Cuomo,

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:51.567
and the way these two yelled at
each other was like watching

00:02:51.567 --> 00:02:54.067
two guys play cards
in the back of a butcher shop.

00:02:54.067 --> 00:02:55.934
-They hated Trump. Hated.
-"Hate"'s your word.

00:02:55.934 --> 00:02:57.834
But clearly --
-No, when you say that a man --

00:02:57.834 --> 00:02:59.501
-But the Inspector General,
two of them,

00:02:59.501 --> 00:03:01.000
said it didn't affect
their work.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:02.167
-You think it's fair?

00:03:02.167 --> 00:03:03.801
-I wouldn't want to be
investigated by anybody,

00:03:03.801 --> 00:03:05.501
and it was the right move
to remove them.

00:03:05.501 --> 00:03:06.701
No, they didn't.

00:03:06.701 --> 00:03:08.167
-By the time they were finished.
-Yes, they did.

00:03:08.167 --> 00:03:09.601
They don't pay any attention
to the platform.

00:03:09.601 --> 00:03:11.868
-I was raised by a guy who would
have corrected the punctuation

00:03:11.868 --> 00:03:13.868
in the party platform.
I'm saying that, that was --

00:03:13.868 --> 00:03:15.767
-Chris, let me explain --
-The guy was the head

00:03:15.767 --> 00:03:17.567
of the A.G. at the time
was his campaign guy.

00:03:17.567 --> 00:03:19.000
-I'm hyperactive
about the probe.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:20.767
Chris, let's be truthful.
Let's be truthful.

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:22.534
-Always. Always.
-Come on, now.

00:03:22.534 --> 00:03:25.167
-Mom!

00:03:25.167 --> 00:03:27.100
The only thing missing
from that conversation

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:29.434
was a few salami rolls
hanging on strings.

00:03:29.434 --> 00:03:31.701
[ Laughter ]

00:03:31.701 --> 00:03:35.400
That interview should have had
a voiceover from Ray Liotta.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:36.367
[ Indistinct arguing ]

00:03:36.367 --> 00:03:37.968
-As far back as I could
remember,

00:03:37.968 --> 00:03:39.734
I always wanted
to be a gangster.

00:03:39.734 --> 00:03:43.767
-And that was all --
That was, like --

00:03:43.767 --> 00:03:48.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:48.167 --> 00:03:52.100
That was, like, not even
a minute into it.

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:54.667
Rudy starts every interview
like he's in hour five

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:56.000
of a police interrogation.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:58.501
"I want to welcome
our next guest, Rudy Giuliani.

00:03:58.501 --> 00:04:01.200
-You got me! I'll tell you
everything you want to know!

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:03.334
And then Cuomo asked Rudy
about the latest bombshell

00:04:03.334 --> 00:04:04.367
in the Russia investigation.

00:04:04.367 --> 00:04:06.400
Trump campaign's chairman Paul
Manafort

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:09.000
shared political polling data
with a business associate

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:10.167
tied to Russian intelligence,

00:04:10.167 --> 00:04:12.434
and that's when Rudy
made a stunning claim.

00:04:12.434 --> 00:04:15.334
He never said the campaign
didn't collude with Russia,

00:04:15.334 --> 00:04:18.234
just that Trump himself
didn't collude with Russia.

00:04:18.234 --> 00:04:20.467
-Now you have Paul Manafort
giving poll data --

00:04:20.467 --> 00:04:22.267
-I never said --
-That winds up leading to

00:04:22.267 --> 00:04:23.300
this coincidence.

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:24.734
-Well, you just misstated
my position.

00:04:24.734 --> 00:04:27.667
I never said there was no
collusion between the campaign

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:29.501
or between people
in the campaign.

00:04:29.501 --> 00:04:31.200
-Yes, you have.
-I have no idea -- I have not.

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:32.534
I said the President
of the United States.

00:04:32.534 --> 00:04:35.267
He said he didn't.
He didn't say nobody.

00:04:35.267 --> 00:04:37.467
How would you know that
nobody in your campaign --

00:04:37.467 --> 00:04:39.767
-He actually did say that,
Rudy. He said nobody.

00:04:39.767 --> 00:04:41.033
-Well, I never said that.
&gt;&gt; And then he said,

00:04:41.033 --> 00:04:42.300
"As far as I know."
-If he said that, he said it

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:44.367
in -- Well, as far as he knows,
that's true!

00:04:44.367 --> 00:04:45.400
-Look at him!

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:46.634
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.634 --> 00:04:50.033
Even he looks surprised
by what he just said.

00:04:50.033 --> 00:04:51.667
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:51.667 --> 00:04:55.467
Either that, or he's got a
binder clip behind his head

00:04:55.467 --> 00:04:57.634
pulling back all of his skin.

00:04:57.634 --> 00:04:58.767
[ Laughter ]

00:04:58.767 --> 00:05:00.868
He looks like a grandpa
at a theme park

00:05:00.868 --> 00:05:03.334
who didn't realize how fast
the roller coaster was.

00:05:03.334 --> 00:05:05.801
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:05.801 --> 00:05:10.534
Also, also, also -- yes.

00:05:10.534 --> 00:05:13.033
You did say
there was no collusion

00:05:13.033 --> 00:05:14.934
and you didn't say it
once or twice.

00:05:14.934 --> 00:05:17.133
You said it a bunch of times.

00:05:17.133 --> 00:05:19.434
-Russian collusion.
Here's what they found.

00:05:19.434 --> 00:05:21.434
Zero. Nada. Nothing.

00:05:21.434 --> 00:05:23.400
If anything, it's proof
there was no collusion.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:26.133
Nobody talked about Russians.
Nobody knew about Russians.

00:05:26.133 --> 00:05:29.767
There was no collusion
with the Russians.

00:05:29.767 --> 00:05:31.601
No collusion with the Russians.

00:05:31.601 --> 00:05:33.067
There was no collusion.

00:05:33.067 --> 00:05:34.767
There was no Russian collusion.

00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:37.033
No Russian collusion. Case over.

00:05:37.033 --> 00:05:38.467
Was there collusion? Come on.

00:05:38.467 --> 00:05:40.300
Nobody believes anymore
there was collusion.

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:43.467
-Think about how much their
argument has changed.

00:05:43.467 --> 00:05:45.934
It went from there were
no contacts with Russians

00:05:45.934 --> 00:05:47.868
to there was no collusion
with Russians

00:05:47.868 --> 00:05:50.167
to we tried to collude,
but nothing came of it

00:05:50.167 --> 00:05:51.834
to collusion is not a crime

00:05:51.834 --> 00:05:53.901
to there was collusion,
but it didn't involve Trump.

00:05:53.901 --> 00:05:56.467
If this keeps going, Rudy
is going to be telling Trump,

00:05:56.467 --> 00:05:59.100
"It's not jail,
it's a gated community."

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:01.234
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:01.234 --> 00:06:03.901
Now...

00:06:03.901 --> 00:06:07.501
We don't -- We don't know.

00:06:07.501 --> 00:06:10.634
We don't know exactly what
Trump's level of involvement was

00:06:10.634 --> 00:06:13.267
in collusion, but we do know
that as a politician

00:06:13.267 --> 00:06:15.133
and president,
Trump has always admired

00:06:15.133 --> 00:06:17.634
Russian President Vladimir Putin
and sought to emulate him.

00:06:17.634 --> 00:06:19.534
Even before he ran
for president,

00:06:19.534 --> 00:06:22.400
he was desperate to
be Putin's friend.

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:25.434
-Do you have a relationship
with Vladimir Putin,

00:06:25.434 --> 00:06:27.033
a conversational relationship?

00:06:27.033 --> 00:06:28.467
-I do have a relationship.

00:06:28.467 --> 00:06:31.701
I spoke indirectly and directly
with President Putin

00:06:31.701 --> 00:06:33.634
who could not have been nicer.

00:06:33.634 --> 00:06:35.767
I was in Moscow
a couple months ago.

00:06:35.767 --> 00:06:37.634
I own the Miss Universe pageant.

00:06:37.634 --> 00:06:40.033
And they treated me so great.

00:06:40.033 --> 00:06:41.734
Putin even sent me a present.

00:06:41.734 --> 00:06:44.267
Beautiful present
with a beautiful note.

00:06:44.267 --> 00:06:46.767
-[ As Trump ] It was a beautiful
note, handwritten,

00:06:46.767 --> 00:06:49.701
and it was delivered by a raven
in the middle of the night.

00:06:49.701 --> 00:06:52.367
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:52.367 --> 00:06:56.300
Just tapped...

00:06:56.300 --> 00:06:59.634
his beak, you know, his beak
tapped, and that woke me up.

00:06:59.634 --> 00:07:01.267
[ Normal voice ]
And we also know that Trump

00:07:01.267 --> 00:07:03.567
has had all kinds of business
entanglements with Russians

00:07:03.567 --> 00:07:05.567
and Putin, in particular,
including the fact that

00:07:05.567 --> 00:07:07.934
as late as the summer of 2016,

00:07:07.934 --> 00:07:11.434
he was in talks with Putin to
build a Trump Tower in Moscow.

00:07:11.434 --> 00:07:13.133
He was even going to
entice Putin

00:07:13.133 --> 00:07:15.400
by giving him an apartment
in the building.

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:17.834
-One of the ideas for that
Trump building,

00:07:17.834 --> 00:07:20.033
according to one of his business
associates,

00:07:20.033 --> 00:07:23.767
was to give the top floor,
the penthouse apartment

00:07:23.767 --> 00:07:27.501
in a 250-apartment block,
to Vladimir Putin,

00:07:27.501 --> 00:07:30.968
the Russian president,
as a way of attracting buyers.

00:07:30.968 --> 00:07:34.067
-Trump's plan was to attract
buyers by telling them

00:07:34.067 --> 00:07:37.767
you get to live in the same
building as Vladimir Putin.

00:07:37.767 --> 00:07:39.734
Can you imagine what it would be
like to have Putin

00:07:39.734 --> 00:07:41.868
as your upstairs neighbor?

00:07:41.868 --> 00:07:43.100
[ Russian accent ] Hello,
would you mind

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:43.901
turning down your music?

00:07:43.901 --> 00:07:45.634
Otherwise I poison your dog.

00:07:45.634 --> 00:07:47.267
[ Laughter ]

00:07:47.267 --> 00:07:52.467
"Okay. I see you
at co-op meeting!

00:07:52.467 --> 00:07:54.834
[ Laughter ]

00:07:54.834 --> 00:07:56.234
[ Normal voice ]
Trump repeatedly denied

00:07:56.234 --> 00:07:58.133
he had any sort of business
relationship with Russia,

00:07:58.133 --> 00:08:00.734
but that line changed
once we found out

00:08:00.734 --> 00:08:03.100
about the deal to build
a Trump Tower in Moscow.

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:05.200
Trump said, "If I did do it,

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:06.767
there would have been
nothing wrong."

00:08:06.767 --> 00:08:09.000
But there would have been
something wrong.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:11.167
It would have violated
the Constitution.

00:08:11.167 --> 00:08:12.868
There's a section
of the Constitution

00:08:12.868 --> 00:08:15.601
called the emoluments clause
that specifically forbids

00:08:15.601 --> 00:08:17.634
the president from taking gifts
from foreigners.

00:08:17.634 --> 00:08:20.133
And we know that because
during the election,

00:08:20.133 --> 00:08:24.400
Donald Trump supporters kept
saying Hillary was breaking it.

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:28.234
-Every foreign gift,
every foreign speech

00:08:28.234 --> 00:08:29.667
while she was...
-It's a big charge.

00:08:29.667 --> 00:08:32.067
-...Senator or Secretary of
State, every one --

00:08:32.067 --> 00:08:34.067
No, it's not a big charge.
It's the U.S. Constitution.

00:08:34.067 --> 00:08:35.667
There's a section
in the Constitution

00:08:35.667 --> 00:08:36.767
called the emoluments clause.

00:08:36.767 --> 00:08:39.534
It says,
"No one, nor their spouse

00:08:39.534 --> 00:08:41.234
can take money from foreigners."

00:08:41.234 --> 00:08:43.767
She has to be guilty
of 70 or 100 counts

00:08:43.767 --> 00:08:45.801
just on that one charge.

00:08:45.801 --> 00:08:48.434
-You think Hillary's guilty
because she had a foundation

00:08:48.434 --> 00:08:50.834
that gave out malaria shots
to kids in Africa?

00:08:50.834 --> 00:08:52.033
Trump had a charity,

00:08:52.033 --> 00:08:55.467
and he used it to buy
two portraits of himself.

00:08:55.467 --> 00:08:57.167
Although when it comes
to Trump portraits,

00:08:57.167 --> 00:08:58.534
this remains my favorite.

00:08:58.534 --> 00:08:59.901
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:59.901 --> 00:09:02.968
Look at that, the difference
between that portrait

00:09:02.968 --> 00:09:05.234
and the actual Donald Trump
is like the difference

00:09:05.234 --> 00:09:06.968
between Spider-Man in the comics

00:09:06.968 --> 00:09:08.767
and the Spider-Man
in Times Square.

00:09:08.767 --> 00:09:10.200
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:14.067
It's the difference between
the Big Mac in the commercial

00:09:14.067 --> 00:09:17.133
and the one you actually get
in your drive-through bag.

00:09:17.133 --> 00:09:18.267
[ Laughter ]

00:09:18.267 --> 00:09:20.334
And on top of that,
Trump and Putin have had

00:09:20.334 --> 00:09:22.767
several private meetings
with no one else in attendance.

00:09:22.767 --> 00:09:25.234
And we have no idea what they
discussed in those meetings.

00:09:25.234 --> 00:09:27.133
The only people who do know
are the Russians

00:09:27.133 --> 00:09:29.167
thanks to note-taking practices
they developed

00:09:29.167 --> 00:09:30.534
during the Soviet era.

00:09:30.534 --> 00:09:31.767
The "Washington Post"
reported yesterday

00:09:31.767 --> 00:09:33.567
the United States
has no detailed record

00:09:33.567 --> 00:09:35.767
of Trump's five face-to-face
interactions with Putin

00:09:35.767 --> 00:09:37.033
over the past two years.

00:09:37.033 --> 00:09:39.000
Russia, on the other hand,
almost certainly does.

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:40.901
The interpreters working
for Soviet leaders

00:09:40.901 --> 00:09:43.567
were trained to take nearly
verbatim stenographic notes.

00:09:43.567 --> 00:09:45.834
Can you imagine how hard it is

00:09:45.834 --> 00:09:48.801
to take verbatim stenographic
notes of Donald Trump?

00:09:48.801 --> 00:09:51.100
Even closed captioning
has a hard time

00:09:51.100 --> 00:09:52.334
following what he's saying.

00:09:52.334 --> 00:09:55.100
-God bless
the United Schtates.

00:09:55.100 --> 00:09:56.234
Thank you very much.

00:09:56.234 --> 00:09:57.133
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:57.133 --> 00:09:59.133
-That's why --

00:09:59.133 --> 00:10:01.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:01.334 --> 00:10:05.467
That's why their argument
keeps changing.

00:10:05.467 --> 00:10:06.634
They don't have an argument,

00:10:06.634 --> 00:10:08.400
and the reality
is slowly sinking in.

00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:10.834
Trump can say he didn't know
he was colluding with Putin

00:10:10.834 --> 00:10:13.300
because Putin hypnotized him,
and Rudy would say --

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:14.968
-As far as he knows,
that's true!

00:10:14.968 --> 00:10:16.834
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:10:16.834 --> 00:10:18.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:18.601 --> 00:10:20.801
♪♪

